35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The car is often empty or dirty when I need it. My weekly trips keep failing.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Misaki, the diary shows Saturdays are triple the use of Tuesdays. The mess is real.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the fixed costs are 280,000 yen. But the fuel is split unevenly.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@All, other groups failed because they had to ask favours constantly. We must avoid that.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, yes. Two people bought most of the fuel. The fixed costs are high.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If my weekly trips collapse, I cannot rely on this. I need a system that protects those slots.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, a fixed day allocation might protect your slots, but it wastes the car on off-days.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, a booking calendar could balance the load, but it requires constant recording.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, recording takes an hour a week. That is too much friction for us.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I agree. The trial of recording every run was too tedious. We need something simpler.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I prefer a system where I know the car is ready and available for my specific needs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, a primary keeper could ensure the car is ready, but who pays for the upkeep?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, if one person keeps it, they bear the burden. The others pay per trip.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, that sounds like asking a favour every time. That is what soured the other groups.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, true. But if the keeper covers costs, the others just pay for what they use.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I am leaning towards a system that guarantees my weekly trips without constant negotiation.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Misaki, a fixed day allocation gives you that guarantee. You hold the car on your days.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@May, that is a fair trade. You pay a fixed share, and you have the car.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, if we agree on fixed days, we stop asking favours. That solves the trust issue.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I agree. Fixed days mean fixed costs. No more guessing who owes what.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
